The three black groups are

* A2  l {A1,A3,B2}
* B3B4 l {A3,B2,A4}
* C1C2 l {B1,B2}

B2 is the only point common to all three.

* 1.W B2 → 2.B B1 forced. W B2 is captured and C1C2B1 l {A1,B2}. A2 l {A1,A3,B2}, B3B4 l {A3,A4,B2} remain alive.
* 1.W B1 → C1C2 in atari on B2. 2.B B2 forced, M = A2 B2 B3 B4 C1 C2 l {A1,A3,A4} and W B1 l {A1}. A1 is suicide for White. 3.W A3/A4 is met by 4.B A4/A1 capturing the white net and 4.B A5 removing the A3–A4 net, restoring ≥1 liberty to M.
* 1.W A3 is self-atari l {A4}. 2.B A4 captures W A3 at once, or 2.B B2 → M l {A1,A4,B1} with W A3 l {A4} → 3.B A4 captures W A3.
* 1.W A4 l {A3,A5}. Best defence 2.B B2 → M l {A1,A3,B1} with W A4 l {A3,A5}. 3.W A1 is met by 4.B B1 capturing W A1, 3.W B1 is met by 4.B A1 capturing W B1, 3.W A3 is illegal suicide on W A4. M keeps A1/A3/B1.
* 1.W A1 l {B1}. 2.B B1 captures W A1 at once.

Every frontier first move is answered by an immediate capture or by the connecting 2.B B2 which unites the three black groups and leaves M with A1,A3,A4 ≥1 liberty while the attacking white stone is left in atari on A1. No opening white move creates a forced double atari that Black cannot answer, so no kill-initiating first move exists.

